+    """QS-26: probabilistic_sortino_ratio and probabilistic_adjusted_sortino_ratio
+    raised ZeroDivisionError on a one-row series while probabilistic_sharpe_ratio
+    returned nan on the same input. The standard error divides by n - 1, and the
+    outcome turned only on whether the base ratio arrived as a numpy scalar,
+    where nan/0 is nan, or as a plain float, where it raises."""
